{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas","id":1204419,"title":"Moonsilver Warstrider ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-07T21:30:55-07:00","id":1204419,"title":"Moonsilver Warstrider ideas?","content":"The Walking Devil Tower very much covers the idea of moonsilver being ferocious and savage. But trying to copy it by caging another behemoth feels cheap, and it feels cheaper to explore a purely mechanical warstrider which somehow possesses similar fury.<br /> <br /> I had the idea for a &quot;mirror match&quot; Warstrider which evokes Szoreny with an Evocation like that Second Edition Ebon Dragon Charm that changes out all of your traits to mirror one target. If you're up against Godzilla, you become Mecha-Godzilla. But it feels more interesting as an NPC antagonist than as a fully-stated PC tool.<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://escaflowne.wikia.com/wiki/Alseides\" target=\"_blank\">Alseides </a>of <i>Escaflowne </i>seems good for moonsilver's affinity for secrecy and transformation, given the invisibility cloak, the liquid-metal weapons, and its transformation into a flying mode. But I'm not feeling a great urge to translate such a thing, and I definitely couldn't submit the work to Onyx Path, which has a rule about &quot;filing off the serial numbers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Escaflowne itself has similar pros and cons, but I find myself unconvinced that a moonsilver warstrider should only be capable of assuming just <i>one </i>alternative animal form. Yet I am not entirely sold on my own plans for a warstrider that gains its own Heart's Blood library from the megafauna you kill with it. Not nearly as much as a suit of articulated plate which transforms the Lunar into a living moonsilver statue, from which state a Lunar could use Towering Beast Shape.<br /> <br /> Something like <a href=\"http://zoids.wikia.com/wiki/Liger_Zero\" target=\"_blank\">Liger Zero</a> (give or take the lion shape) is promising. A moonsilver warstrider whose Evocations take the form of different sets of jade attachments, which it switches between to change its strengths to fit its current situation.<br /> <br /> I've considered a moonsilver answer to Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation, based on <i>Overwatch's</i> Bastion and <i>Starcraft's</i> Siege Tanks. One of its Evocations transforms the warstrider into an immobile artifact ballista which doesn't suffer from the Slow tag, allowing a pilot to rain down volleys of massive, destructive bolts even before using a following Evocation to fire a shot like a Lightning Ballista or Implosion Bow. Might also have a mobile Tank Mode.<br /> <br /> The tricky part of the Liger Zero and Bastion ideas seems to be balancing an artifact which could essentially act like multiple artifacts in one.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I wasn't happy with my attempts to design a <a href=\"http://gurrenlagann.wikia.com/wiki/Lagann\" target=\"_blank\">Lagann</a>-like warstrider which specialized in combining with other warstriders. I could understand the appeal of designing a Voltron-like team of warstriders with the power to combine together, but not a lone warstrider which couldn't do anything special without any other warstrider. Not even if it could also transform into a suit of armor for a dinosaur or behemoth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T03:55:02-07:00","id":1204493,"title":"","content":"What about... a Lunar with a kind of relentless pursuer and stalking hunter theme? I'm thinking powers like being able to inject foes (even things like other warstriders) with poisonous moonsilver, that it then becomes capable of sensing and following after no matter how far they go. Maybe a fighting style of starting off with attacks from afar to weaken foes, that build up as they're chased down, culminating in a major deadly strike once range is closed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T06:53:09-07:00","id":1204529,"title":"","content":"I'd had something on the back-burner, never really developed it much. It was <b>Centimane</b>, a warstrider made with white jade and moonsilver, intended for throwing big stuff at enemies. <br /> <br /> The first Evocation, <i>Hundred Eyes of Gyges</i>, would boost your Aim actions and allow you to remove the penalty from throwing an object with the Improvised tag. <br /> <br /> The second, <i>Hundred Grips of Briareos</i>, would raise the warstrider's effective Strength for feats of strength, and would raise it even more on ones where you throw something. Visually represented as sprouting extra hands as needed, which grasp at the object and grant additional leverage.<br /> <br /> The final Evocation, <i>Kottos' Tomb of Boulders</i>, also requires Cascade of Cutting Terror, and buries the foe under a hail of massive missiles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-08-2018, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T07:35:27-07:00","id":1204539,"title":"","content":"A wolf-themed Warstrider who functions around commanding a pack of lesser wolf-golems.<br /> <br /> Love the image of a moonsilver Wolf Pack bringing down a behemoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T08:13:49-07:00","id":1204554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1204493#post1204493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about... a Lunar with a kind of relentless pursuer and stalking hunter theme? I'm thinking powers like being able to inject foes (even things like other warstriders) with poisonous moonsilver, that it then becomes capable of sensing and following after no matter how far they go. Maybe a fighting style of starting off with attacks from afar to weaken foes, that build up as they're chased down, culminating in a major deadly strike once range is closed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see at least two problems, and a way to work around them.<br /> <br /> The first problem is that liquid moonsilver might be poisonous to organic life, but not so much to machines, and warstriders are so varied in their mechanisms that you can't count on most of them having anything like a circulatory system for spreading poison.<br /> <br /> The second problem is that extended operation is a weakness for warstriders, as it racks up their maintenance requirements or dips straight into outright causing damage that needs major repairs.<br /> <br /> The solution might be to tap into moonsilver's affinity for dreams and otherworldly realms. With an Evocation similar to Emerald Chevalier's Eternal Cataphract Empowerment, the pilot enters a fugue dream-state while hunting her chosen quarry, which makes it easier to hunt that target for a long time but which makes it harder to respond or interact with anything else. More and more of her Evocations would be about taking herself bodily (along with the warstrider) out of the physical realm where others can interfere with her hunt.<br /> <br /> Her moonsilver poison isn't meant to damage another warstrider, but rather works as an agent that imposes the same disconnection from reality, cutting that prey off from others who might be able to help it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1204529#post1204529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd had something on the back-burner, never really developed it much. It was <b>Centimane</b>, a warstrider made with white jade and moonsilver, intended for throwing big stuff at enemies.<br /> <br /> The first Evocation, <i>Hundred Eyes of Gyges</i>, would boost your Aim actions and allow you to remove the penalty from throwing an object with the Improvised tag.<br /> <br /> The second, <i>Hundred Grips of Briareos</i>, would raise the warstrider's effective Strength for feats of strength, and would raise it even more on ones where you throw something. Visually represented as sprouting extra hands as needed, which grasp at the object and grant additional leverage.<br /> <br /> The final Evocation, <i>Kottos' Tomb of Boulders</i>, also requires Cascade of Cutting Terror, and buries the foe under a hail of massive missiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's neat.<br /> <br /> I don't know why Solar Thrown doesn't have an actual &quot;throw multiple projectile attacks&quot; Charm anymore; CoCT is really just throwing one projectile that you copy with magic.<br /> <br /> But Centimane could definitely make use of the Solar Thrown Charm that allows it to disarm multiple warstriders/weapon-wielding giants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T08:19:13-07:00","id":1204556,"title":"","content":"Moonsilver doesn't have to be poisonous <i>to warstriders</i> to be poisonous.<br /> <br /> Although, something tells me that molten metal writhing its way around inside you is going to hurt regardless of whether you have veins for it to travel through; it might even hurt <i>more</i> if you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-08-2018, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T08:32:27-07:00","id":1204561,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1204556#post1204556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moonsilver doesn't have to be poisonous <i>to warstriders</i> to be poisonous.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bYeah, but, y'know, I suggested that it would be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1204554#post1204554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first problem is that liquid moonsilver might be poisonous to organic life, but not so much to machines, and warstriders are so varied in their mechanisms that you can't count on most of them having anything like a circulatory system for spreading poison.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSee, my thinking was that it would be something that would interact with warstriders in a manner equivalent to poison, following along with moonsilver's capacity for poisonous enchantments. It's not something limited to the nature of the target, but imposed by the magic of the moonsilver. That may or may not take the form of something literal and physical, like a liquefied moonsilver crawling around inside of a 'strider's mechanisms and gumming them up or corroding them, or it could be something a bit more metaphysical.<br /> <br /> \u200bCertainly, I would see that would be the kind of Evocation that could emerge from the spirit of moonsilver warstrider that was designed or applied particularly to the purpose of hunting other warstriders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The solution might be to tap into moonsilver's affinity for dreams and otherworldly realms. With an Evocation similar to Emerald Chevalier's Eternal Cataphract Empowerment, the pilot enters a fugue dream-state while hunting her chosen quarry, which makes it easier to hunt that target for a long time but which makes it harder to respond or interact with anything else. More and more of her Evocations would be about taking herself bodily (along with the warstrider) out of the physical realm where others can interfere with her hunt.<br /> <br /> Her moonsilver poison isn't meant to damage another warstrider, but rather works as an agent that imposes the same disconnection from reality, cutting that prey off from others who might be able to help it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those sound like neat approaches to the idea.<br /> <br /> The fun thing about Evocations is that either approach could be taken to the basic concept, and both could exist in the setting at the same time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T01:09:38-07:00","id":1204808,"title":"","content":".... I had a completely different thought when seeing that title.<br /> <br /> And now I want to see a Moonsliver transforming Warstrider....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T01:36:46-07:00","id":1204810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1204539#post1204539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A wolf-themed Warstrider who functions around commanding a pack of lesser wolf-golems.<br /> <br /> Love the image of a moonsilver Wolf Pack bringing down a behemoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first thought was something a bit like that but instead of a pack leader what about o brood mother. A warstrider that <b>CREATES </b>other combatants.<br /> Kind like how the Distaff creates thread puppets","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T08:36:56-07:00","id":1204873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1204808#post1204808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now I want to see a Moonsliver transforming Warstrider....</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of my past games, the only Moonsilver warstrider that ever showed up was an &quot;all-terrain combat vehicle&quot; that had modes for running, burrowing, flight, and aquatic maneuvers in addition to its humanoid combat mode. It basically had five shapes that it could change into to change up its movement types and weapons loadout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T17:07:52-07:00","id":1205016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackwingedheaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1204873#post1204873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In one of my past games, the only Moonsilver warstrider that ever showed up was an &amp;quot;all-terrain combat vehicle&amp;quot; that had modes for running, burrowing, flight, and aquatic maneuvers in addition to its humanoid combat mode. It basically had five shapes that it could change into to change up its movement types and weapons loadout.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though practically speaking, it would seem to have only two modes, since there would be no point distinguishing the \u201crunning\u201d, burrowing, swimming, or flying modes from each other.<br /> <br /> It wouldn\u2019t try to fly underwater or swim underground or burrow into the sky. The most mechanical expression the differences would need is requiring an action or mote cost for changing the means of locomotion, and specifying any difference in speed for each. <br /> <br /> Well, maybe the burrowing form would have massive drills it could use for weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T00:08:46-07:00","id":1205114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1205016#post1205016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though practically speaking, it would seem to have only two modes, since there would be no point distinguishing the \u201crunning\u201d, burrowing, swimming, or flying modes from each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel like this is, or <i>should</i> be true. Changing shape to something that swims like a fish <i>should</i> feel pretty different from changing shape to something that flies like a bird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T05:40:01-07:00","id":1205149,"title":"","content":"Weird image that i have in mind is of some sort of The Blob/T-1000 Moonsilver Warstrider, capable of changing forms, flowing through places or adversaries, engulfing them (possibly turning into pearls and additional sources of power), shaping a variety of melee weapons, maybe generating a small army of warrior automata, among other crazy bits to go with the &quot;living metal tsunami&quot; theme of sorts.<br /> <br /> Random aside, has anyone considered the possibility of a level 5 artifact armor or shield that upgrades into Warstrider form with one of its high-level evocations? It's something that i've been musing upon but not yet tinkered with as i just started reading on Warstriders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-10-2018, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T05:47:40-07:00","id":1205152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1205149#post1205149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird image that i have in mind is of some sort of The Blob/T-1000 Moonsilver Warstrider, capable of changing forms, flowing through places or adversaries, engulfing them, shaping a variety of melee weapons, maybe generating a small army of warrior automata, among other crazy bits to go with the &quot;living metal tsunami&quot; theme of sorts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Might as well go crazy at least once.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Random aside, has anyone considered the possibility of a level 5 artifact armor or shield that upgrades into Warstrider form with one of its high-level evocations?<br /> <br /> It something that i've been musing upon but not yet tinkered with as i just started reading on Warstriders. </div> </div> </div>Easy. Tony Stark\u2019s Iron Man armor.<br /> <br /> One of its higher Evocations is the Hulk Buster additions.<br /> <br /> Arms of the Chosen also has that blue jade armor that turns you into a Legendary Size flying elemental dragon, as some precedent. Though one probably wants to make the Iron Man armor a piece of First Age Artifice, for extra benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:27:55-07:00","id":1205171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1205016#post1205016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though practically speaking, it would seem to have only two modes, since there would be no point distinguishing the \u201crunning\u201d, burrowing, swimming, or flying modes from each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>The balanced combat mode was humanoid, the faster running mode turned it into a wolf, the burrowing mode was a giant mole with drill-paws, the swimming mode was a killer whale, and the flying mode was a giant hawk. Practical, nothing. It was more <i>awesome</i> that way. XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:24:06-07:00","id":1205246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1205016#post1205016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baaldam[/B]] Weird image that i have in mind is of some sort of The Blob/T-1000 Moonsilver Warstrider, capable of changing forms, flowing through places or adversaries, engulfing them, shaping a variety of melee weapons, maybe generating a small army of warrior automata, among other crazy bits to go with the &quot;living metal tsunami&quot; theme of sorts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. Might as well go crazy at least once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking a little more on the imagery/theme i suggested, it has crossed my mind that the Vodak Hekatonkheire under Gethamane could provide some inspiration for Evocations.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1205016#post1205016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baaldam[/B]]Random aside, has anyone considered the possibility of a level 5 artifact armor or shield that upgrades into Warstrider form with one of its high-level evocations?<br /> <br /> It something that i've been musing upon but not yet tinkered with as i just started reading on Warstriders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Easy. Tony Stark\u2019s Iron Man armor.<br /> <br /> One of its higher Evocations is the Hulk Buster additions.<br /> <br /> Arms of the Chosen also has that blue jade armor that turns you into a Legendary Size flying elemental dragon, as some precedent. Though one probably wants to make the Iron Man armor a piece of First Age Artifice, for extra benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never really thought of the Hulk Buster add-ons as a warstrider, but certainly works for inspiration. The blue jade armor sounds good too and might fit better with my current interests (not artifacts as works of supernatural craft per se, but god-blooded Inheritance as reflected manifestations of the spirit parent's panoply, so to speak) than a literal armor or warstrider would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:08:58-07:00","id":1205298,"title":"","content":"Tony\u2019s armor doesn\u2019t need to be First Age Artifice to have the magitech aesthetic, mind you. Just to have abilities which would break the setting if any other Artifact of the same level and type had it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T06:42:41-07:00","id":1205570,"title":"","content":"I wonder about a warstrider that could have been made in the image of the Fair Folk; I'm picturing one that is lithe and graceful with an unusually ornate and detailed face, having been constructed with the aid of raksha nobles in the planning, and tinker gnomes in the actual construction. Possibly having an intention of specifically going to fight in the Wyld and/or against the Fair Folk, running on a kind of theme of deception and luring them into thinking that it's one of their own. Maybe Evocations based on having beguiling dances that draw beings of the Wyld close to admire its beauty, and then slaughtering them in displays that they're hard pressed to recognise as attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T08:27:28-07:00","id":1205605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1205570#post1205570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder about a warstrider that could have been made in the image of the Fair Folk; I'm picturing one that is lithe and graceful with an unusually ornate and detailed face, having been constructed with the aid of raksha nobles in the planning, and tinker gnomes in the actual construction. Possibly having an intention of specifically going to fight in the Wyld and/or against the Fair Folk, running on a kind of theme of deception and luring them into thinking that it's one of their own. Maybe Evocations based on having beguiling dances that draw beings of the Wyld close to admire its beauty, and then slaughtering them in displays that they're hard pressed to recognise as attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of those themes and tricks make think a bit of Black Claw Style, what is certainly curious too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T08:34:39-07:00","id":1205609,"title":"","content":"Black Claw is more about attacking somebody while coming across as the victim, even to the person that you're attacking. I'm talking about something more like a cross between turning the Fair Folk's game back upon them, and being a kind of microcosm for what Creation represents to them; something that can lure enemies in with its beauty, while being hazardous to them.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm also thinking that it could have a pinnacle Charm a bit akin to the highest power of Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation, in which at the apex of its dance, it unleashes a wave of calcification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T08:50:51-07:00","id":1205613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1205609#post1205609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Claw is more about attacking somebody while coming across as the victim, even to the person that you're attacking. I'm talking about something more like a cross between turning the Fair Folk's game back upon them, and being a kind of microcosm for what Creation represents to them; something that can lure enemies in with its beauty, while being hazardous to them.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm also thinking that it could have a pinnacle Charm a bit akin to the highest power of Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation, in which at the apex of its dance, it unleashes a wave of calcification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good point about how Mara's style goes somewhat farther - and lower - in its &quot;agression under a masquerade&quot; gimmick than what you have in mind, that is more in line with luring and entrancing the opposition toward ambush/doom.<br /> <br /> Something that also came to mind, though again, probably far from a ideal simile, is Sozen, the Cataphract of Keys, the demon that never was, from the armors chapter of Arms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:06:41-07:00","id":1205882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackwingedheaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1205171#post1205171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The balanced combat mode was humanoid, the faster running mode turned it into a wolf, the burrowing mode was a giant mole with drill-paws, the swimming mode was a killer whale, and the flying mode was a giant hawk. Practical, nothing. It was more <i>awesome</i> that way. XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel good about a moonsilver warstrider which is designed to transform into animal shapes but can't assume as many animal forms as a Lunar pilot.<br /> <br /> Can anyone sell me on that idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T03:43:23-07:00","id":1205979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1205882#post1205882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel good about a moonsilver warstrider which is designed to transform into animal shapes but can't assume as many animal forms as a Lunar pilot.<br /> <br /> Can anyone sell me on that idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when i conceived i Quicksilver Tsunami - the liquid moonsilver warstrider - one of the things that crossed my mind was, in engulfing adversaries and sealing them inside &quot;Elsewhere Cysts/Pearls&quot; it gaining the use to their forms for its use, with access to memories, or their dreamscapes as &quot;pocket wyld zones/sanctums&quot; for use in who knows in what utterly bizarre ways, as possible upgrades. How does that sound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T06:22:54-07:00","id":1206006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1205979#post1205979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, when i conceived i Quicksilver Tsunami - the liquid moonsilver warstrider - one of the things that crossed my mind was, in engulfing adversaries and sealing them inside &quot;Elsewhere Cysts/Pearls&quot; it gaining the use to their forms for its use, with access to memories, or their dreamscapes as &quot;pocket wyld zones/sanctums&quot; for use in who knows in what utterly bizarre ways, as possible upgrades. How does that sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stealing Raksha power sounds more appropriate to the anti-Wyld warstrider proposed above. I think an amorphous, liquid-metal warstrider has enough potential without having the ability to assume defined shapes or steal foreign magic.<br /> <br /> I also think this doesn\u2019t really address my discomfort regarding limited animal shapeshiftering in moonsilver warstriders like Escaflowne.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:26:15-07:00","id":1206041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206006#post1206006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stealing Raksha power sounds more appropriate to the anti-Wyld warstrider proposed above. I think an amorphous, liquid-metal warstrider has enough potential without having the ability to assume defined shapes or steal foreign magic.<br /> <br /> I also think this doesn\u2019t really address my discomfort regarding limited animal shapeshiftering in moonsilver warstriders like Escaflowne.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, do Lunars still have a core beast shape/warform as in previous editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:04:13-07:00","id":1206088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206041#post1206041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an aside, do Lunars still have a core beast shape/warform as in previous editions?</div> </div> </div> </div>They still start with one animal form without Heart's Blood, and right now that's the only advantage of the spirit shape (regarding shapeshifting, at least). As it should be, because we don't want people choosing totems based on what is most advantageous in a fight for cheaper or faster transformation.<br /> <br /> DBT is being split apart. The Hybrid form is the package of mutations, and you can have multiple hybrid shapes. The War Form is the massive stat-buff you can only use while in Hybrid form.<br /> <br /> Some part of those buffs is still useful in a warstrider - better meeting the strength minimums, boosts to movement actions... And some mutations are still useful inside a cockpit, like Enhanced Senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-12-2018, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:21:48-07:00","id":1206096,"title":"","content":"I feel as though a warstrider based on being able to liquefy and engulf an otherworldly being could be the kind of thing that functions on the logic of why Karvara could be caged in moonsilver as a more general thing. It loses the kind of sheer power that the N/A Artifact got from being able to wholly contain the reality-shredding abomination, but makes up for it with more diverse applications. Fluidity, consumption, containing and harnessing otherworldly powers and diversity all being parts of the moonsilver wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206088#post1206088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They still start with one animal form without Heart's Blood, and right now that's the only advantage of the spirit shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo, remember there are going to be Charms with a keyword that lets you learn them with an alternative Attribute if they're fitting to your spirit shape. So Lunars with venomous totems will be able to learn Charms to produce venom with either Stamina or... I want to say Wits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T13:20:41-07:00","id":1206143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206041#post1206041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an aside, do Lunars still have a core beast shape/warform as in previous editions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Edition. Previous edition. 1e made you buy it if you were casteless, and you didn't start out with it in a narrative sense - you had to hunt, kill, and eat somewhere in the character history in 1e if you had Finding the Spirit's Shape. The text mentioned this as &quot;gaining the shape fairly&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 04-12-2018, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T15:24:13-07:00","id":1206177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206096#post1206096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though a warstrider based on being able to liquefy and engulf an otherworldly being could be the kind of thing that functions on the logic of why Karvara could be caged in moonsilver as a more general thing. It loses the kind of sheer power that the N/A Artifact got from being able to wholly contain the reality-shredding abomination, but makes up for it with more diverse applications. Fluidity, consumption, containing and harnessing otherworldly powers and diversity all being parts of the moonsilver wheelhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure who you\u2019re addressing, so it\u2019s hard to know exactly what you\u2019re arguing. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, remember there are going to be Charms with a keyword that lets you learn them with an alternative Attribute if they're fitting to your spirit shape. So Lunars with venomous totems will be able to learn Charms to produce venom with either Stamina or... I want to say Wits. </div> </div> </div>I remember, but I was strictly talking about physical combat shapeshifting rather than Charms and Favored Attributes.<br /> <br /> The Totem keyword seems less about rewarding you for picking \u201cthe optimum\u201d spirit shape of a fast bird or a giant monster, and more about not punishing you for having only four Favored Attributes to choose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T15:31:56-07:00","id":1206178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206177#post1206177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure who you\u2019re addressing</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnybody who was arguing against the idea of a quicksilver warstrider that could take the powers of raksha?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it\u2019s hard to know exactly what you\u2019re arguing.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat a quicksilver warstrider that could take the powers of raksha is perfectly viable as a concept for a moonsilver warstrider, on the basis of about two or three qualities of moonsilver and warstriders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T16:08:54-07:00","id":1206188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206178#post1206178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAnybody who was arguing against the idea of a quicksilver warstrider that could take the powers of raksha?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bThat a quicksilver warstrider that could take the powers of raksha is perfectly viable as a concept for a moonsilver warstrider, on the basis of about two or three qualities of moonsilver and warstriders.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might shake out a bit more easily to have powers reminiscent of raksha, on account of how raksha power schemes have changed or might change (the prior developers were kicking around simplified power clusters like WoD powers that aren't Gifts, but that, too, is up in the air) and will probably not be sufficiently detailed to show strong themes for a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T16:25:35-07:00","id":1206193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206178#post1206178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAnybody who was arguing against the idea of a quicksilver warstrider that could take the powers of raksha?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bThat a quicksilver warstrider that could take the powers of raksha is perfectly viable as a concept for a moonsilver warstrider, on the basis of about two or three qualities of moonsilver and warstriders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think people were talking more of stylistic preferences than Moonsilver's apropriateness for such or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T16:55:03-07:00","id":1206198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206193#post1206193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think people were talking more of stylistic preferences than Moonsilver's apropriateness for such or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHmm, I want to clarify more, and make sure that I don't inadvertently mischaracterize somebody.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs I saw it, Sunder was saying that it was unnecessary to combine the elements of liquid metal and appropriating raksha powers in a single warstrider, without disputing the idea that either was fitting for moonsilver.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat I had in mind as something that would unify them was the image of a warstrider whose structure and mythos could allow it to, on an ad hoc and impermanent basis, encase other beings in its moonsilver body, in a manner akin to what was permanently done to Karvara. I don't think I actually made that clear.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd I also do now see my response up there as being a bit unhelpful, and starting to erroneously construe Sunder as having argued the ideas being fitting to moonsilver at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T18:44:17-07:00","id":1206222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206198#post1206198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHmm, I want to clarify more, and make sure that I don't inadvertently mischaracterize somebody.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs I saw it, Sunder was saying that it was unnecessary to combine the elements of liquid metal and appropriating raksha powers in a single warstrider, without disputing the idea that either was fitting for moonsilver.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat I had in mind as something that would unify them was the image of a warstrider whose structure and mythos could allow it to, on an ad hoc and impermanent basis, encase other beings in its moonsilver body, in a manner akin to what was permanently done to Karvara. I don't think I actually made that clear.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd I also do now see my response up there as being a bit unhelpful, and starting to erroneously construe Sunder as having argued the ideas being fitting to moonsilver at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's it.<br /> <br /> Wasn't suggesting it was a poor fit for moonsilver, since I suggested it might fit easily into the Evocations of the anti-fae warstrider suggested above.<br /> <br /> I merely suggested that the amorphous liquid warstrider already had so much potential to play with in the realm of being amorphous, and I'd like to see someone exhaust those possibilities first before looking to add another gimmick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T19:06:57-07:00","id":1206230,"title":"","content":"I'm of two minds.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the one is the idea where a liquid form is an almost purely aesthetic thing, to serve as a basis for the image of why it's able to so freely encompass and release targeted beings. The base form of the thing is basically a highly versatile cage.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the <i>other</i> is the idea that such an aesthetic being the basis of the power is the specific reason to make it part of general powers reflecting a liquid form. That might be the kind of thing that lends itself to a pinnacle Charm on top of other things that are otherwise largely focused on the liquid metal, or even to a branching path in the Evocations (since, being at least Artifact 5, it can be home to many).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T19:08:48-07:00","id":1206232,"title":"","content":"A predatory warstrider that steals parts and evocations from other warstriders or similarly sized beasts it encounters/devours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T19:24:45-07:00","id":1206240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206232#post1206232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A predatory warstrider that steals parts and evocations from other warstriders or similarly sized beasts it encounters/devours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I talked to Robert Vance about a warstrider stealing stuff from other warstriders, and he seemed to think that was too powerful.<br /> <br /> Warstrider Evocations tend be more powerful than the Charms of living creatures with similar size. It's because of the First Age Artifice changing the balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T11:06:57-07:00","id":1206532,"title":"","content":"I think that I'd like to see Warstriders in general as the pillars of a Chronicle, and not just very-expensive stuff.<br /> <br /> My favorite suggestion so far, for example, would be the Zoids, including Liger Zero. Keep the idea of growing in synchronicity with your Zoidstrider. Keep the idea of gaining new gear for it (though a little more pointy and a little less gunny). Replace the idea of a tournament presided by people in satellites. Et voila, you've got some pretty decent cornerstones for the foundation of a fun Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T12:10:33-07:00","id":1206567,"title":"","content":"But on the subject of Liger Zero, how do you balance variable Evocations in any artifact?<br /> <br /> Like my idea for a version of Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation which has a Immobile Ballista Turret Mode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T16:17:45-07:00","id":1206712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206567#post1206567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on the subject of Liger Zero, how do you balance variable Evocations in any artifact?<br /> <br /> Like my idea for a version of Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation which has a Immobile Ballista Turret Mode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Balancing Evocations isn't something I've got down pat yet. I'm sure there would be a couple of paths for each 'strider's Evocation tree, which could represent the deepening connection and the addition of equipment and improvements. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T20:49:22-07:00","id":1206778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206567#post1206567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on the subject of Liger Zero, how do you balance variable Evocations in any artifact?<br /> <br /> Like my idea for a version of Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation which has a Immobile Ballista Turret Mode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know if i have said it before, but every time i see that thing's name i end up missreading as &quot;Ligier Zero&quot; and thinking of <a href=\"https://orig00.deviantart.net/b43c/f/2008/253/f/6/the_mad_sun_of_malfeas_by_kiyo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> guy, possibly mixed with <a href=\"https://tfwiki.net/wiki/Mirage_(G1)/toys\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-14-2018, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T21:01:50-07:00","id":1206784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1205149#post1205149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird image that i have in mind is of some sort of The Blob/T-1000 Moonsilver Warstrider, capable of changing forms, flowing through places or adversaries, engulfing them (possibly turning into pearls and additional sources of power), shaping a variety of melee weapons, maybe generating a small army of warrior automata, among other crazy bits to go with the &quot;living metal tsunami&quot; theme of sorts.<br /> <br /> Random aside, has anyone considered the possibility of a level 5 artifact armor or shield that upgrades into Warstrider form with one of its high-level evocations? It's something that i've been musing upon but not yet tinkered with as i just started reading on Warstriders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funnily enough, a recurring warstrider my circle encounters on the regular is the &quot;Protean Lord Annihilator,&quot; a metal blob warstrider based off the Dominator from Overman King Gainer.The evocations such a beastly weapon has are largely based off of its ability to freely meld itself into any weapon or tool the pilot can think of, and shrink or grow in size as needed. I'm glad to know that I'm not the only one to think of that application for Moonsilver, and its great fun to have it show up and be a goofy albeit legitimate threat each time it shows up.<br /> <br /> Sadly, I can't help you in your request, as my Circle more or less decided that warstriders are a no-no for personal based tool or weapon evocations, considering how powerful they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T21:12:28-07:00","id":1206787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206784#post1206784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Funnily enough, a recurring warstrider my circle encounters on the regular is the &quot;Protean Lord Annihilator,&quot; a metal blob warstrider based off the Dominator from Overman King Gainer.The evocations such a beastly weapon has are largely based off of its ability to freely meld itself into any weapon or tool the pilot can think of, and shrink or grow in size as needed. I'm glad to know that I'm not the only one to think of that application for Moonsilver, and its great fun to have it show up and be a goofy albeit legitimate threat each time it shows up.<br /> <br /> Sadly, I can't help you in your request, as my Circle more or less decided that warstriders are a no-no for personal based tool or weapon evocations, considering how powerful they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's what level 5 artifacts can sort of be a excuse for! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But to each their own preferences, can accept that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T22:24:11-07:00","id":1207164,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for how to flesh out the Mirror Match warstrider idea, based on another idea I had which didn't seem like enough by itself.<br /> <br /> Before you unlock the Evocation to mirror another opponent of similar size, the attunement bonus of the warstrider is to mirror yourself.<br /> <br /> It not only looks like a larger version of you, it also apes your weapons and armor.<br /> <br /> Thus, the warstrider has no standard weapons, and possibly poor soak and hardness. But on the plus side, you can use your regular artifact weapons and armor with all the benefits of Legendary Size, and the warstrider becomes compatible with your Martial Arts Styles even if they're not normally armor-compatible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T10:53:24-07:00","id":1207329,"title":"","content":"I think Moonsilver is a good place for non-human shaped warstriders like the centaur one. I don't know that I would like a super mutable one designed to match any shape a Lunar could assume (why not just be a giant lunar?), But I like the idea of some Lunar building a warstriders you need to be in animal form to operate because screw you, Dragonblooded. Also, so you can train your pet god-wolf to operate your wolf shaped warstriders for maximum shenanigans.<br /> <br /> I also see some opportunities to play with Moonsilver's dreams-and-Nightmares schtick. A giant war machine that burns itself into the nightmares of those who witness it on the battlefield, that imposes intimacies of fear and then feeds on them to repair itself or deploy across distances by traveling through dreams? Maybe some charms for doing the thing where &quot;we fight in a dream and you wake up bleeding where I stabbed you,&quot; only to buildings and city walls? Apex evocation puts whole armies into an enchanted sleep? I dunno, I feel like there's room there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T13:54:25-07:00","id":1207400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1207329#post1207329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Moonsilver is a good place for non-human shaped warstriders like the centaur one.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, the centaur one suggests otherwise.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to build a warstrider in the form of a bird, I would use blue jade. Black jade for an aquatic warstrider. Green jade would be quite fine for a warstrider in the form of a wolf or cat or snake.<br /> <br /> But if I wanted to build a warstrider that could hunt from the skies or beneath the waves or under the earth, I would use moonsilver.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know that I would like a super mutable one designed to match any shape a Lunar could assume (why not just be a giant lunar?) </div> </div> </div>Because only warstriders can make devastating actions, and warstrider Evocations are on a different level from other Evocations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also see some opportunities to play with Moonsilver's dreams-and-Nightmares schtick. A giant war machine that burns itself into the nightmares of those who witness it on the battlefield, that imposes intimacies of fear and then feeds on them to repair itself or deploy across distances by traveling through dreams? Maybe some charms for doing the thing where &quot;we fight in a dream and you wake up bleeding where I stabbed you,&quot; only to buildings and city walls? Apex evocation puts whole armies into an enchanted sleep? I dunno, I feel like there's room there... </div> </div> </div>That sounds cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T21:03:54-07:00","id":1217581,"title":"","content":"I was trying to design a Niobraran warstrider that harnessed the power of moonsilver to dominate the boundary between the sea and the sky... but rather than a waterborne version of Emerald Chevalier's hit-and-run tactics, it's really more of a First Age artifice jet-boat. It doesn't need legs to swim, or arms to attack.<br /> <br /> A little more promising is an idea for the Deliberative's response -- a winged warstrider spear-fisher that can pierce through the water's surface, shooting arrows freely at underwater targets or bodily diving into the water before returning to the sky. Again, the power of moonsilver would be bent towards mastering the boundary between sea and sky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T07:22:47-07:00","id":1217654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1206230#post1206230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u200bOn the one is the idea where a liquid form is an almost purely aesthetic thing, to serve as a basis for the image of why it's able to so freely encompass and release targeted beings. The base form of the thing is basically a highly versatile cage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe a long string of connected cages. Some sort of Moonsilver ... Train.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T08:39:16-07:00","id":1217677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1217654#post1217654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe a long string of connected cages. Some sort of Moonsilver ... Train.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think you\u2019re being clever, but you earn only a bronze star for such a brazen taunt. You might get a better score if you can figure out my riddle; I will not cop(per) out by revealing the answer myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T08:54:59-07:00","id":1217680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1217581#post1217581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to design a Niobraran warstrider that harnessed the power of moonsilver to dominate the boundary between the sea and the sky... but rather than a waterborne version of Emerald Chevalier's hit-and-run tactics, it's really more of a First Age artifice jet-boat. It doesn't need legs to swim, or arms to attack.<br /> <br /> A little more promising is an idea for the Deliberative's response -- a winged warstrider spear-fisher that can pierce through the water's surface, shooting arrows freely at underwater targets or bodily diving into the water before returning to the sky. Again, the power of moonsilver would be bent towards mastering the boundary between sea and sky.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about a Ephemeral Cloud Jellyfish so to speak? Now there's a sea critter that could visually mesh well with sky, imho, producing cyclone tentacles and lightning stingers like Frost-Thorn Knuckles produces blades of ice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-11-2018, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T10:19:02-07:00","id":1217701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1217680#post1217680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a Ephemeral Cloud Jellyfish so to speak? Now there's a sea critter that could visually mesh well with sky, imho, producing cyclone tentacles and lightning stingers like Frost-Thorn Knuckles produces blades of ice.</div> </div> </div> </div>A jellyfish warstrider made of black and/or blue jade wouldn\u2019t need moonsilver to lend it ferocity; sea storms are plenty ferocious. If it\u2019s graceful rather than tenacious (\u201cemphermal cloud\u201d doesn\u2019t evoke soak-enhancement), those colors of jade can do that too.<br /> <br /> Your proposed machine would operate around the water\u2019s surface, but isn\u2019t actually concerned with or dependent on the boundary of the water\u2019s surface.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-11-2018, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T14:09:34-07:00","id":1217772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1217701#post1217701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A jellyfish warstrider made of black and/or blue jade wouldn\u2019t need moonsilver to lend it ferocity; sea storms are plenty ferocious. If it\u2019s graceful rather than tenacious (\u201cemphermal cloud\u201d doesn\u2019t evoke soak-enhancement), those colors of jade can do that too.<br /> <br /> Your proposed machine would operate around the water\u2019s surface, but isn\u2019t actually concerned with or dependent on the boundary of the water\u2019s surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it goes into the sky too, flying as a <b>cloud</b>, playing on the cycle of waters above and below...well, it open possiblities.<br /> <br /> But yeah, my focus was probably far more on the boundary between sea and sky - and coming and going between them through imagery of the cycle of evaporation, clouds and rain than worrying about specific magic materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T14:53:00-07:00","id":1217783,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think your idea is about boundaries at all.<br /> <br /> Does it dive violently from the air into the water without falling damage? Does it shoot arrows through the surface like it wasn\u2019t there, or automatically take aim at anything that breaks the surface? Does it move faster on the water\u2019s surface than below or above it? Does it reflexively duck under the water\u2019s surface to use it as a shield?<br /> <br /> Does it use its ability to pierce the water\u2019s surface as a prerequisite to the ability to pierce armor and walls?<br /> <br /> Does it expand upon its power of liminality when in Shadowlands and Wyld Zones that serve as the boundary between Creation and other worlds? Or to create mirror-portal entrances that exit out of the water\u2019s surface?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T16:53:15-07:00","id":1217825,"title":"","content":"Regardless of whether it's sufficiently moonsilver-y or not, we should at least acknowledge that a flying/swimming jellyfish warstrider with tornado-tentacles and lightning-stingers is a baller idea.<br /> <br /> That said, I think as described it's at least somewhat liminal, existing as it does in that weird class of things that Exalted thinks are different, air/blue-jade stuff (clouds, flying) and water/black-jade stuff (sea, swimming), but that observably are closely related (water, buoyancy). At a minimum some sort of moonsilver &quot;adapter&quot; to make the blue and black jade play nice together seems fitting.<br /> <br /> Add in some neat advanced evocations that take advantage of this essential nature in more metaphorical ways and I think that would clinch it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T17:17:48-07:00","id":1217830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1217825#post1217825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of whether it's sufficiently moonsilver-y or not, we should at least acknowledge that a flying/swimming jellyfish warstrider with tornado-tentacles and lightning-stingers is a baller idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about it as a warstrider, but as a behemoth (or an elemental with Legendary Size), that is indeed most exciting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I think as described it's at least somewhat liminal, existing as it does in that weird class of things that Exalted thinks are different, air/blue-jade stuff (clouds, flying) and water/black-jade stuff (sea, swimming), but that observably are closely related (water, buoyancy). At a minimum some sort of moonsilver &quot;adapter&quot; to make the blue and black jade play nice together seems fitting.<br /> <br /> Add in some neat advanced evocations that take advantage of this essential nature in more metaphorical ways and I think that would clinch it. </div> </div> </div>But does the whole picture in your head make sense to be something that isn't resonant with Dragon-Blooded, but instead resonant with Lunars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T21:29:34-07:00","id":1218145,"title":"","content":"Some disjointed ideas that are incomplete on their own but which don't necessarily need to fit together in a single moonsilver warstrider:<br /> <br /> <br /> * Being constructed around the bones of a behemoth which could (unlike Karvara) actually die. The warstrider is therefore much less willful and dangerous.<br /> <br /> <br /> * A dangerous super-mode which consumes one of the pilot's health levels every turn. Lunar Exalted can use this power the most, since (traditionally) they have the best Ox-Bodies and they're unmatched at combat-time regeneration.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Attunement bonus &quot;miens&quot; like the Unison armor, but only two (since Unity's first is superfluous for a warstrider). The first mien reduces the warstrider's Soak and Hardness in return for a greater Speed bonus and +1 to Evasion. The second mien instead eschews the Evasion bonus and sacrifices Speed for greater brute toughness and strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T13:53:13-07:00","id":1224428,"title":"","content":"We were talking about moonsilver warstriders which could skirt around the need for infrastructure. The Walking Devil Tower actually has a number of advantages in that area.<br /> <br /> As long as the pilot defeats, kills, and consumes a behemoth, a battle group with might, or an opponent with higher Essence, it can use Eat the Heart of God and Undying Behemoth Rebirth to recover from damage incurred during the battle.<br /> <br /> Karvara also has a truly ridiculous number of health levels, allowing it to take more damage from battle and a lack of maintenance before it cannot operate any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:16:43-07:00","id":1232421,"title":"","content":"How many people would want to see a Noble warstrider inspired by <i>Macross'</i> Valkyries and the Gundams which are capable of transforming into &quot;waverider&quot; jet modes?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking it would be built as light -- or possibly even lighter! -- as Godspeed Vanguard, with comparably low Soak, Hardness, and Health Levels. But without the same Speed bonus.<br /> <br /> Its standard armament would include at least one straight sword, a shield, a one-handed crossbow, and a two-handed crossbow. Special back-mounted armatures would allow it to reflexively swap between these weapons as per Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation, but without the auto-reloading functions or the ability to double-aim.<br /> <br /> The warstrider's first Evocation is to transform into its flying mode. While in this mode, it can freely ascend or -- by extending its rocket-legs down in a bird-like fashion -- hover in place. Its Speed bonus is at least doubled.<br /> <br /> But it can't perform Martial Arts or Thrown attacks, it cannot parry with any Ability, nor perform any action requiring hands. Its larger crossbow becomes forward fixed and therefore cannot be used to attack any opponent the warstrider is moving away from, while its smaller crossbow becomes backwards-fixed and cannot be used against any character towards which the warstrider is moving.<br /> <br /> Becoming capable of the diving and flyby attacks enjoyed by Ascendant Nova Phoenix requires another Evocation, where the flying mode warstrider can make use of the sword affixed to its nose.<br /> <br /> The warstrider would include something like Emerald Chevalier's Indomitable Charger Focus for combining a Rush action with an Aim action, as well as an Evocation for improving its ability to dodge attacks as long as it keeps moving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T13:57:57-07:00","id":1232478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1232421#post1232421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many people would want to see a Noble warstrider inspired by <i>Macross'</i> Valkyries and the Gundams which are capable of transforming into &quot;waverider&quot; jet modes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would want to see something that comes from anybody's creativity and inspiration. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I like Macross, but I'd be most interested in what would come of what it means to you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T07:10:24-07:00","id":1232616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1204419-moonsilver-warstrider-ideas?p=1232478#post1232478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would want to see something that comes from anybody's creativity and inspiration. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I like Macross, but I'd be most interested in what would come of what it means to you.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Macross'</i> Valkyries have always represented two things, to me and to their pilots: The freedom of the skies, and the protection of one's people.<br /> <br /> Boiled down to one word: Liberty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}